# The production API base, baked into every ordinary `npm run build`.
#
# Before this file existed, VITE_API_BASE had no default at all — every
# build was offline unless someone remembered to prefix the build command
# with it by hand. DEPLOY.md documents an unset VITE_API_BASE as a
# deliberate rollback state ("the game plays offline, no server at all"),
# which is exactly right for that one purpose and exactly wrong as the
# silent default every ordinary build fell back to the moment anyone typed
# a bare `npm run build` — which is what shipped tonight, twice, with no
# account, no leaderboard and no payments working at all, and nothing on
# screen said so.
#
# Vite loads this automatically for `vite build` (production mode) and lets
# an explicit shell value override it, so the rollback path in DEPLOY.md §8
# still works exactly as written — `VITE_API_BASE= npm run build` still
# produces an offline build on purpose. What changes is the ACCIDENT: doing
# nothing now ships the working game, not the disconnected one.
VITE_API_BASE=https://dovefall-api.bgkaranja.workers.dev
